      "sourceMarkdown": "# K2 Unit 1: Our New School\n\n## Unit Metadata\n- Level: K2\n- Course Line: English Learning\n- Unit Number: 1\n- Unit Theme: Our New School\n- Status: Draft for classroom use\n- Source Basis: Current generated Power Up data + web language classification scaffold\n\n## Unit Focus\nTalk about school.\n\n## Unit Learning Outcomes\n- talk about school\n- describe where objects are using prepositions\n- ask questions using Where is / Where are...?\n- ask and answer using This is / These are\n- read for correct information\n- be kind\n\n## Power Up Alignment\n- Power Up level: Level 1\n- Power Up unit: Unit 1\n- Main source pages: see per-day Source blocks\n- Source audio: see per-day Source blocks\n- Notes: Standard 4-week Power Up flow with Mission Extend / Showcase Week.\n\n## 4-Week Teaching Flow\n### Week 1\n- Day 1: PU L1 — Unit opener and Mission set up\n- Day 2: PU L2 — Vocabulary 1 presentation\n- Day 3: PU L3 — Story with new language presented in context\n- Day 4: PU L4 — Language practice 1 and Mission Stage 1\n- Day 5: Mission Extend — Mission Extend 1\n\n### Week 2\n- Day 1: PU L5 — Vocabulary 2 presentation and song\n- Day 2: PU L6 — Language practice 2 and Mission Stage 2\n- Day 3: PU L7 — Cross-curricular presentation and video\n- Day 4: PU L8 — Cross-curricular consolidation and Mission Stage 3\n- Day 5: Mission Extend — Mission Extend 2\n\n### Week 3\n- Day 1: PU L9 — Literature - story focus\n- Day 2: PU L10 — Literature - response to story and social and emotional skills\n- Day 3: PU L11 — A1 Movers preparation\n- Day 4: PU L12 — Unit review and Mission in action\n- Day 5: Mission Extend — Mission Extend 3 / Showcase Preparation\n\n### Week 4\n- Day 1: Showcase — Showcase Lesson 1\n- Day 2: Showcase — Showcase Lesson 2\n- Day 3: Showcase — Showcase Lesson 3\n- Day 4: Showcase — Showcase Lesson 4\n- Day 5: Showcase — Showcase Lesson 5\n\n\n## Teacher / Design Guidance\n- Child-facing content for this unit is driven by the current web page + classification scaffold. The Power Up source pages, audio tracks, and the language summaries above are the primary inputs.\n- The week-by-week flow above reflects the current generated data. Course designers may adjust day-to-day roles without changing the PU lesson mapping.\n- Old Power Up teacher notes, classroom management guidance, and unit design rationale (from earlier markdown source) belong in this section, NOT in child-facing fields.\n\n## Open Design Tasks\n- Circle Time: add topic + song for each day.\n- Phonics: add daily phonics mini-lesson content (K1 starts in Unit 1 L7; K2/K3 have phonics embedded).\n- Story: add daily story / book connection.\n- Media Extend / Mission Extend / Mini Mission: design teacher-led follow-up activities.\n- Showcase: design week 4 student-led project.\n\n## Review Issues\nSee per-day `## Review Issues` sections in the day files. Abstract umbrella items (colours, family, school, etc.) are kept here for human decision.\n",
