        "sourceMarkdown": "# Day 2, Week 2\n\n## Day Metadata\n- Level: K2\n- Unit Number: 1\n- Unit Theme: Our New School\n- Day: 2\n- Week: 2\n- Day Type: Power Up\n- Power Up Lesson: PU L6\n- Lesson Role: Language practice 2 and Mission Stage 2\n\n## Circle Time\n### Topic\nTBD (Power Up theme: Our New School)\n\n### Song\nTBD\n\n### Teacher Notes\nUse Circle Time to warm up the lesson theme. Keep it oral, visual, and routine-based. Model any target sentence as a whole chunk the children can repeat.\n\n## CLIL Class\n### Lesson Outcome\nBy the end of the lesson, learners will be able to ask and answer what singular and plural nouns are.\n\n### Source\n- Teacher's Book: TB p11\n- Pupil's Book: PB p11\n- Activity Book: AB p6\n- Pupil's Book Audio:\n  - Track 1.16: `u01/PU_SB_BE_L1_U01_Pg011_tr_016(1.16).mp3`\n  - Track 1.17: `u01/PU_SB_BE_L1_U01_Pg011_tr_017(1.17).mp3`\n\n### New Keywords\n- TBD\n\n### Recycled Keywords\n- TBD\n\n### Target Sentences\n- What's this? It's a ...\n- What are these? They're ...\n\n### Activities and Games\n1. TBD\n2. TBD\n3. TBD\n\n### Teacher / Design Guidance\n**Mission (Power Up — adapt for classroom flow)**\n\nL6: Mission Stage 2: Words\n\nLearners find objects in the classroom they do not know in English, ask the teacher, then draw and write the new word for later use.\n\n**Power Up teaching focus**\n\nThe original Power Up lesson is the source of truth for this day. The current page shows the auto-classified keywords and target sentences; the teacher can model them as words and as sentence chunks without inventing new content.\n\n## Phonics\n### Content\nTBD\n\n### Teacher Notes\nTBD\n\n## Story\n### Book / Story\nTBD\n\n### Teacher Notes\nTBD\n\n## Review Issues\n### Needs Extension\n- Umbrella item: classroom\n  - Original source: Recycled Language\n  - Suggested concrete words from current scaffold: book, crayon, teacher, bag, classroom, pencil, school, rubber\n  - Decision needed: choose whether to teach this as a category word or replace it with concrete child-facing items.\n\n### Source Issues\n- None for this day.\n",
