        "sourcePath": "/Users/Lucia/Desktop/eastie_curriculum_project/content/curriculum/k-language-canonical-v0_1/k3/unit_01_a_day_on_the_farm/week_01/day_04.md",
        "sourceMarkdown": "# Day 4, Week 1\n\n## Day Metadata\n- Level: K3\n- Unit Number: 1\n- Unit Theme: A Day on the Farm\n- Day: 4\n- Week: 1\n- Day Type: Power Up\n- Power Up Lesson: PU L4\n- Lesson Role: Language practice 1 and Mission Stage 1\n\n## Circle Time\n### Topic\nTBD (Power Up theme: A Day on the Farm)\n\n### Song\nTBD\n\n### Teacher Notes\nUse Circle Time to warm up the lesson theme. Keep it oral, visual, and routine-based. Model any target sentence as a whole chunk the children can repeat.\n\n## CLIL Class\n### Lesson Outcome\nwill be able to ask and answer questions and write about what people are doing, using the present continuous.\n\n### Source\n- Teacher's Book: TB p9\n- Pupil's Book: PB p9\n- Activity Book: AB p9\n- Pupil's Book Audio:\n  - Track 1.12: `u01/PU_SB_BE_L2_U01_Pg009_tr_012(1.12).mp3`\n  - Track 1.13: `u01/PU_SB_BE_L2_U01_Pg009_tr_013(1.13).mp3`\n\n### New Keywords\n- they aren't.\n- clean (v)\n- do homework\n- put on\n- scissors\n- take off\n\n### Recycled Keywords\n- sports and hobbies\n- boots\n- crayon\n- drink\n- eat\n- hand\n- ice cream\n- kitchen\n- lemonade\n- wash\n\n### Target Sentences\n- Are you reading a book?\n- No, I'm not (reading a book).\n- No, I'm not.\n- I'm doing my homework.\n- Is she playing tennis?\n- Yes, please.\n- Yes, she is.\n- She's playing tennis.\n- Are they putting on their boots?\n- No, thank you.\n- They're taking off their boots.\n\n### Activities and Games\n1. TBD\n2. TBD\n3. TBD\n\n### Teacher / Design Guidance\n**Mission (Power Up — adapt for classroom flow)**\n\nL4: Mission Stage 1: Make your chart\n\nLearners create their own daily routine chart using the vocabulary they have learned. They draw and label their daily activities.\n\n**Power Up teaching focus**\n\nThe original Power Up lesson is the source of truth for this day. The current page shows the auto-classified keywords and target sentences; the teacher can model them as words and as sentence chunks without inventing new content.\n\n## Phonics\n### Content\nTBD\n\n### Teacher Notes\nTBD\n\n## Story\n### Book / Story\nTBD\n\n### Teacher Notes\nTBD\n\n## Review Issues\n### Needs Extension\n- None for this day.\n\n### Source Issues\n- None for this day.\n",
