        "sourceMarkdown": "# Day 1, Week 2\n\n## Day Metadata\n- Level: K3\n- Unit Number: 1\n- Unit Theme: A Day on the Farm\n- Day: 1\n- Week: 2\n- Day Type: Power Up\n- Power Up Lesson: PU L5\n- Lesson Role: Vocabulary 2 presentation and song\n\n## Circle Time\n### Topic\nTBD (Power Up theme: A Day on the Farm)\n\n### Song\nTBD\n\n### Teacher Notes\nUse Circle Time to warm up the lesson theme. Keep it oral, visual, and routine-based. Model any target sentence as a whole chunk the children can repeat.\n\n## CLIL Class\n### Lesson Outcome\nwill have practised the language through song.\n\n### Source\n- Teacher's Book: TB p10\n- Pupil's Book: PB p10\n- Activity Book: AB p10\n- Pupil's Book Audio:\n  - Track 1.14: `u01/PU_SB_BE_L2_U01_Pg010_tr_014(1.14).mp3`\n\n### New Keywords\n- get dressed\n- get up\n- have a shower\n- have breakfast\n- toothbrush\n- toothpaste\n- towel\n- wake up\n- clean your teeth\n- (get) dry\n- Time for us to...\n\n### Recycled Keywords\n- food and drink\n- sports and hobbies\n- get\n- go\n- run\n- sit down\n- imperatives\n- present simple\n\n### Target Sentences\n- TBD\n\n### Activities and Games\n1. TBD\n2. TBD\n3. TBD\n\n### Teacher / Design Guidance\n**Power Up teaching focus**\n\nThe original Power Up lesson is the source of truth for this day. The current page shows the auto-classified keywords and target sentences; the teacher can model them as words and as sentence chunks without inventing new content.\n\n## Phonics\n### Content\nTBD\n\n### Teacher Notes\nTBD\n\n## Story\n### Book / Story\nTBD\n\n### Teacher Notes\nTBD\n\n## Review Issues\n### Needs Extension\n- Umbrella item: present continuous\n  - Original source: Recycled Language\n  - Suggested concrete words: TBD (no children found in earlier K lessons)\n  - Decision needed: choose whether to teach this as a category word or replace it with concrete child-facing items.\n\n### Source Issues\n- None for this day.\n",
