        "sourceMarkdown": "# Day 4, Week 3\n\n## Day Metadata\n- Level: K3\n- Unit Number: 1\n- Unit Theme: A Day on the Farm\n- Day: 4\n- Week: 3\n- Day Type: Power Up\n- Power Up Lesson: PU L12\n- Lesson Role: Unit review and Mission in action\n\n## Circle Time\n### Topic\nTBD (Power Up theme: A Day on the Farm)\n\n### Song\nTBD\n\n### Teacher Notes\nUse Circle Time to warm up the lesson theme. Keep it oral, visual, and routine-based. Model any target sentence as a whole chunk the children can repeat.\n\n## CLIL Class\n### Lesson Outcome\nwill have revised the language in the unit and presented their daily routine chart to the class.\n\n### Source\n- Teacher's Book: TB p17\n- Pupil's Book: PB p17\n- Activity Book: AB p17\n\n### New Keywords\n- TBD\n\n### Recycled Keywords\n- unit language\n\n### Target Sentences\n- TBD\n\n### Activities and Games\n1. TBD\n2. TBD\n3. TBD\n\n### Teacher / Design Guidance\n**Mission (Power Up — adapt for classroom flow)**\n\nL12: Mission in action\n\nLearners present their daily routine chart to the class using the present simple and times (o'clock). They answer questions from their classmates.\n\n**Power Up teaching focus**\n\nThe original Power Up lesson is the source of truth for this day. The current page shows the auto-classified keywords and target sentences; the teacher can model them as words and as sentence chunks without inventing new content.\n\n## Phonics\n### Content\nTBD\n\n### Teacher Notes\nTBD\n\n## Story\n### Book / Story\nTBD\n\n### Teacher Notes\nTBD\n\n## Review Issues\n### Needs Extension\n- None for this day.\n\n### Source Issues\n- None for this day.\n",
